# the text form of a PE/COFF model
#
# the file as the model holds it, in file order: the DOS header, the file header, the
# optional header with its data directories, the section headers, the relocations of each
# section, the symbol table with its auxiliary records, then the typed structures of the
# data directories. every record and field takes the name llvm-readobj gives it, so the
# output lines up field by field with what llvm-readobj prints for the same file, in the
# LLVM output style of LLVM 23, the release the tables are generated from. a value with a
# name prints its name and its number, from the tables of the machine the file is for. a
# directory the reader held raw prints its bytes raw. the dump prints what the model holds
# and decodes nothing the reader did not.

